// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 22-surface-syntax
// facility: spec/22 §1 byte-literal (lexical ill-formedness); conf.byte-literal-empty-parse-error
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.syntax-error (static)
//
// `b""` is ill-formed: the byte-literal production requires at least one
// byte, since an empty array literal has no element to take `u8` from.

fn main()
{
    auto b = b"";
}
